  "description": "The back of the hand. Between the first and second metacarpals the first web space holds the first dorsal interosseous and, deeper, adductor pollicis; a needle passed straight through it reaches the palmar skin. The radial artery crosses the anatomical snuffbox and dives between the two heads of the first dorsal interosseous near the bases of the metacarpals. Dorsal branches of the superficial radial nerve and the dorsal venous network lie in the subcutaneous tissue.",
